## Status Rules

| Status | Gate |
|--------|------|
| `VERIFIED` | ≥2 distinct sources (after content dedupe) **AND** resolvable member findings **AND** `verification_status: RUN` with cited verification evidence |
| `PROBABLE` | ≥1 distinct source; reasoning recorded; verification not yet run |
| `CANDIDATE` | Nominated (e.g. lexical similarity) — investigate, never present as established |

## Independence Rule

**Repeated copies of the same content are ONE source, never independent evidence.** A pattern supported by the same text appearing in five files has one source, not five. Check that multiple findings are genuinely independent before counting them.

**Single occurrence is never a recurring-pattern conclusion** — one event, however suggestive, stays out of this register or is recorded as a CANDIDATE with an explicit note.

